# StudyForge REST API

GET    /assignments/:id                  Get one assignment
PATCH  /assignments/:id                  Update (status, title, due_date, etc.)
DELETE /assignments/:id
PATCH  /assignments/:id/status           Move between Kanban columns (drag-and-drop)

POST   /assignments/:id/breakdown        AI: split assignment into subtasks + time estimates
```

## AI Tutor
```
POST   /courses/:id/tutor/messages       Send a message to the course-scoped tutor
GET    /courses/:id/tutor/messages       Get chat history
```

## Skills & Learning Items (Growth Mode)
```
GET    /skills                           List user's skills
POST   /skills                           Add a skill

GET    /learning-items                   List learning items (Kanban board data)
POST   /learning-items                   Create learning item
GET    /learning-items/:id
PATCH  /learning-items/:id               Update (status, link to skill/assignment)
DELETE /learning-items/:id
PATCH  /learning-items/:id/status        Move between Kanban columns
```

## Career Goals & Roadmap
```
GET    /career-goals                     List saved goals
POST   /career-goals                     Create goal from a job posting

POST   /career-goals/:id/analyze         AI: compare goal vs. current skills → gap analysis
GET    /career-goals/:id/roadmap         Get generated roadmap
POST   /career-goals/:id/roadmap/regen   Regenerate roadmap
```

## Weekly Summaries
```
GET    /summaries                        List past weekly summaries
GET    /summaries/latest                 Most recent AI-generated summary
POST   /summaries/generate               Manually trigger generation (else runs on a cron)
```

---

## Conventions

- **Auth**: all routes except `/auth/signup` and `/auth/login` require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- **Pagination**: list endpoints accept `?page=1&limit=20`, return `{ data, page, total }`.
- **Errors**: `{ error: { code, message } }` with standard HTTP status codes (400/401/403/404/422/500).
- **Status fields**: `assignments.status` ∈ `todo | in_progress | review | done`; `learning-items.status` ∈ `want_to_learn | learning | practicing | mastered`.
- **AI endpoints** (`/breakdown`, `/tutor/messages`, `/analyze`, `/roadmap`, `/summaries/generate`) are async-friendly — consider returning a `202 Accepted` with a job id if generation takes >2–3s, and a `GET /jobs/:id` for polling.
